###2026.04.13.01
- Fix: Docker folder ``update all`` and ``force update`` now arm the post-update reconcile window from the global UI dispatch path, so collapsed folder rows keep polling fresh runtime state even when the host dialog callback path is delayed or skipped.
- Quality: Docker bulk-update trace writers now recover from invalid cached localStorage payloads instead of dropping new trace entries, so support bundles can capture the actual update dispatch path during troubleshooting.


###2026.04.12.06
- Fix: Docker runtime rows, folder state, and container interactions.
- Quality: Release automation, CI smoke coverage, and packaging guards.


###2026.04.12.05
- Fix: Docker folder update rows now trust refreshed runtime state during the post-update reconcile window, so `update all` no longer leaves stale `apply update` folder badges behind after the server state has already cleared.


###2026.04.12.04
- Quality: Republished the Docker diagnostics bundle build under a new dev package version so Unraid can pull the rendered-state and bulk-update trace support-bundle changes.


###2026.04.12.03
- Fix: Docker runtime rows, folder state, and container interactions.
- UX: Settings workspace layout, section flows, and table behavior.
- Fix: Diagnostics surfaces, issue reports, and support bundle coverage.
- Quality: Release automation, CI smoke coverage, and packaging guards.
- Docs: Project documentation and support guidance.


###2026.04.12.02
- Diagnostics: Support bundles now include the last persisted Docker-page rendered-state snapshot and a recent Docker bulk-update trace, so Settings-page exports can still show what the Docker UI actually rendered after an update flow.
- Diagnostics: The Docker page now records visible folder/member row action text, expanded state, and missing folder-class counts into a support-bundle snapshot to help isolate stale row repaint issues from correct runtime state.
- Quality: Added regression coverage for the new Docker support-bundle telemetry collectors and their wiring into the Settings diagnostics export path.


###2026.04.12.01
- Fix: Docker member-row runtime sync now recovers direct folder rows through the canonical direct-member resolver when host DOM updates strip folder-specific row classes, so bulk-update repaints still clear stale `apply update` badges without a full page refresh.
- Quality: The Docker preview action runtime now falls back from folder-class selectors to direct member recovery before giving up on a row repaint, which hardens update-state sync against host row mutations after bulk updates.
- Regression guard: Added coverage for the direct-member-row fallback path in the Docker update-status regression suite.


###2026.04.11.05
- Fix: Docker folder bulk-update reconciliation now survives the host Docker page redraw that lands after the update dialog completes, so stale `apply update` badges clear without a full page refresh.
- Quality: FolderView Plus now replays the post-update runtime sync from the Docker folder-render event during a short reconcile window instead of relying only on early timer backstops.
- Maintenance: Refreshed the tracked JavaScript performance baseline after accepting the additional Docker bulk-update reconciliation logic.


###2026.04.11.04
- Fix: Docker runtime rows, folder state, and container interactions.
- Quality: Release automation, CI smoke coverage, and packaging guards.
- Docs: Project documentation and support guidance.


###2026.04.11.03
- Fix: Docker folder bulk-update backstop refreshes now pull fresh runtime state directly from FolderView Plus after the host update dialog completes, so stale `apply update` badges clear even when the host list itself lags behind.
- Quality: The Docker bulk-update recovery path now falls back to the debounced host list refresh only if the direct runtime-state sync fails.
- Regression guard: Updated the Docker bulk-update dialog tests to cover direct runtime-state backstop refreshes as well as the legacy host callback path.


###2026.04.11.02
- Fix: Docker folder `update all` and `force update` actions now arm delayed refresh backstops after the host update dialog opens, so stale `apply update` badges clear even when the host modal does not fully reconcile the list immediately.
- Quality: FolderView Plus now wires the Docker action runtime to the debounced list refresh queue for this bulk-update path instead of relying only on the modal callback.
- Regression guard: Added coverage for the Docker bulk-update dialog refresh callback and backstop refresh scheduling.


