###2026.03.30.14
- Fix: Preserve Docker `State.Updated` from the hydrated full runtime payload so folder member rows and folder/root-folder summaries stop getting stuck on `up-to-date` while those containers actually have updates available.
- Fix: Keep lightweight `mode=state` refreshes cheap while still carrying forward the most recent known update state instead of dropping it during Docker runtime info merges.
- Regression guard: Assert the Docker runtime info merge prefers `source.info.State.Updated` from the full payload and only falls back to the previous cached value when the lightweight state payload omits it.


###2026.03.30.13
- Fix: Preserve Docker `State.Updated` from the hydrated full runtime payload so folder member rows and folder/root-folder summaries stop getting stuck on `up-to-date` when those containers actually have updates available.
- Fix: Keep lightweight `mode=state` refreshes cheap while still carrying forward the most recent known update state instead of dropping it back to `null` during runtime merges.
- Regression guard: Assert the Docker runtime info merge prefers `source.info.State.Updated` from the full payload and only falls back to the previous cached value when the lightweight state payload omits it.


###2026.03.30.12
- Fix: Restore the Docker page after the collapsed update-summary refactor by resolving advanced-list mode inside the shared folder update-column renderer instead of referencing an out-of-scope runtime variable during bootstrap.
- Fix: Prioritize the dedicated Docker runtime banner host so fatal runtime diagnostics render at the top of the page instead of dropping to the bottom canvas area.
- Regression guard: Assert the shared folder update-column renderer reads Docker advanced mode locally, and assert fatal-banner host resolution honors selector priority for the dedicated Docker banner host.


###2026.03.30.11
- Fix: Reuse one folder update-column renderer across first paint and runtime hydration so collapsed Docker folders and root folders keep surfacing child container updates without regressing the performance budget.
- Fix: Apply the same host-margin row-centering override to VM folder rows so the VM Application column keeps single-row folder content vertically centered like Docker.
- Regression guard: Assert the shared folder update-column renderer is used by both folder creation and collapsed runtime refresh, and assert the VM row CSS clears host bottom-margin drift.


###2026.03.30.10
- Fix: Rebuild collapsed Docker folder update columns from hydrated runtime container data so folder and root-folder rows show `Update ready` when child containers have updates available, even while the branch is collapsed.
- Fix: Keep the collapsed-folder refresh path aligned with the existing `apply update` and `force update` folder actions instead of leaving the folder row stuck on the lightweight first-paint `up-to-date` state.
- Regression guard: Assert the runtime folder-row refresh path owns the update column and refreshes collapsed folder update state from runtime cache without requiring the folder to be expanded.


###2026.03.30.09
- Fix: Restore the modern folder editor bootstrap after the new accent preview swatch change by defining `accentEnabled` and `accentColor` inside `updateLiveSummary()` before that code touches the live preview chips.
- Fix: Keep the new accent swatch in the editor live preview insights without crashing hydration when the modern editor loads.
- Regression guard: Assert that `folder.editor.preview.js` computes the accent values inside `updateLiveSummary()` before updating `#fvSwatchAccent` and `#fvAccentSwatchItem`.


