- Fix: Bound the Docker and VM `Add Folder` page actions onto the live runtime so inline page buttons still work even when the host page expects global handlers.
- Quality: Moved the shared runtime diagnostics bridge into the common runtime module and added architecture guards so Docker and VM runtime failures stay visible without tripping the file-size ratchet.

###2026.03.26.18
- UX: Refined settings and on-screen update messaging for clarity and consistency.
- Quality: Strengthened release automation and regression guards to prevent note drift.


###2026.03.26.17
- Feature: Roll up the promoted `dev` line since main `2026.03.25.31`, including the modern folder editor rollout with grouped sections, live preview, richer icon handling, and stronger runtime/bootstrap wiring.
- Fix: Resolve the promoted editor regressions across save/bootstrap flow, member reorder preview sync, tab and settings-block layouts, inheritance controls, and light, dark, and Azure theme rendering.
- UI/UX: Refine folder and settings surfaces with stronger title accents, shared outline treatment, larger editor field controls, improved light-theme readability, and cleaner row action button chrome.
- Quality: Expand regression coverage with editor settings-contract checks, runtime theme guards, real browser smoke interactions, and remote raw publish validation for release artifacts.


###2026.03.26.16
- Fix: The shared theme resolver no longer hard-forces the Unraid Azure host theme into the dark compatibility path, so the new folder editor now follows the actual page luminance instead of rendering a mismatched dark shell on Azure.
- Fix: Azure and other non-black named host themes now fall back to computed surface brightness for folder editor theme classification, keeping light host pages on the light editor palette.
- Regression guard: Updated the resolver contract test so only explicit black themes are pinned dark while transparent-surface and light-host inference stays enforced.


###2026.03.26.15
- UI/UX: Removed the boxed square chrome from the row action buttons in the basic settings tables so the standard actions render as clean orange icons instead of outlined mini-buttons.
- UI/UX: Kept the trailing overflow `...` action boxed so the expandable action affordance still reads as a separate control.
- Regression guard: Added a layout assertion covering the unboxed action-button rule for non-overflow row actions.


###2026.03.26.14
- Fix: The settings page now exports the host theme name like the folder editor so white and other light themes enter the correct readable settings palette on the basic page.
- Fix: The shared theme resolver now ignores transparent root backgrounds and no longer hard-forces grey-named themes dark, preventing white-theme settings tables from inheriting unreadable dark tokens.
- Regression guard: Added resolver and settings-page bootstrap assertions to lock the light-theme classification path and prevent another unreadable basic-page regression.


###2026.03.26.13
- Fix: Hardened the modern folder editor field sizing with force-win input rules and class-based inherited-row hiding so health and status controls no longer collapse into tiny clipped placeholders on the live page.
- Fix: Added direct white-theme settings table overrides for nested folder metadata, pin/runtime chips, and empty-state status or alert chips so those cells stay readable even when host page styles outrank the softer token path.
- Regression guard: Extended the folder editor and settings light-theme layout assertions to cover the forced input widths, inherited-row hide rule, and direct readability overrides.


###2026.03.26.12
- Fix: Moved the settings page white-theme breadcrumb, nested metadata, and empty-chip colors onto resolver-applied semantic tokens so light themes no longer fall back to the unreadable dark palette.
- UI/UX: Enlarged the folder editor `Use global` inherit control so the label no longer clips into a tiny `Use g` pill in the modern settings blocks.
- Regression guard: Added runtime token and layout assertions covering the settings semantic palette plus the larger inherit button sizing.


###2026.03.26.11
- Fix: Re-themed the light settings page tree meta, nested folder hints, and neutral status or alert chips so white themes keep readable folder text and empty-state indicators.
- UI/UX: Increased the modern folder editor field control sizes so text, number, select, and textarea inputs are easier to read while editing settings blocks.
- Regression guard: Added light-theme settings contrast and modern editor control sizing assertions to keep these readability fixes from regressing.


###2026.03.26.10
- UX: Removed the duplicate `Using global` inherit control from inherited folder-editor rows so only the inherited-default notice remains visible.
- UI/UX: Shrunk the blue inherited-default badge so it reads as a compact notice instead of a large pill next to the field title.


###2026.03.26.09
- UX: Tightened modern folder editor inheritance notices so `Using global` renders as a compact blue info label instead of a large gray control.
- UI/UX: Applied the orange editor outline treatment across both light and dark modern folder editor surfaces, including cards, controls, settings blocks, and the hero/icon framing.
- Fix: Re-themed the Members section table to use editor surface tokens so light themes no longer render the member list as a flat gray slab.


###2026.03.26.08
- Fix: Restyled inherited folder-editor notices so `Using global` reads as a compact blue info label instead of a full gray button.
- Fix: Extended the modern folder editor orange outline treatment across both light and dark themes, including control borders, hero icon framing, and the remaining settings blocks.
- Fix: Re-themed the Members section table to use the editor surface tokens so light themes no longer render the member list as a flat gray slab.


