###2026.03.25.62
- UX: Collapse the folder editor bootstrap diagnostics by default behind a `Bootstrap diagnostics` disclosure so routine editing stays clean while full runtime details remain available for troubleshooting.
- Regression guard: Enforce that the modern editor startup begins only after late runtime helpers like `folderHierarchyState` are declared, preventing future bootstrap-order regressions from creeping back in unnoticed.


###2026.03.25.61
- Fix: Defer the modern folder editor startup bootstrap until the end of `folder.js`, so saved-folder hydration no longer executes before later runtime helpers like `folderHierarchyState` are initialized.
- Regression guard: Lock the deferred `startFolderEditorRuntime()` bootstrap path into the modern editor smoke and nesting guards so early-start TDZ failures do not regress.


###2026.03.25.60
- Fix: Hoist `updateForm` into a function declaration so the modern editor bootstrap can safely call it before later layout helpers finish loading, preventing the `updateForm` initialization crash during saved-folder hydration.
- Regression guard: Lock the hoisted `updateForm` bootstrap shape into the modern editor smoke and nesting guards so the late `const updateForm` path does not regress.


###2026.03.25.59
- Fix: Promote `normalizeParentFolderId` to a plain top-level editor helper so modern validation can run before the folder hierarchy module is initialized, preventing the remaining parent-folder bootstrap crash before hydration.
- Regression guard: Lock the direct parent-id helper into the modern editor smoke and nesting guards so the late hierarchy alias does not regress.


###2026.03.25.58
- Fix: Delay modern folder editor shared helper API creation until the folder hierarchy helpers are initialized, preventing the early `normalizeParentFolderId` bootstrap crash before hydration.
- Regression guard: Lock the lazy shared-editor bootstrap path into the folder editor guards so eager helper initialization does not regress.


###2026.03.25.57
- Fix: Delay modern folder editor preview API creation until its helper functions are initialized, preventing the early `getIncludedMemberNames` bootstrap crash before hydration.
- Regression guard: Lock the lazy modern preview bootstrap path into the folder editor smoke test so eager preview initialization does not slip back in.


###2026.03.25.55
- Fix: Move the folder editor runtime boot into a page-owned script loader so `Folder.page` can force fresh modern or legacy editor scripts into the active xmenu window on every open.
- Quality: Lock the new injected runtime boot path into the folder page architecture and security guards so the editor no longer depends on passive bottom-of-page script tags.


###2026.03.25.54
- Fix: Scope the modern and legacy folder editor runtimes so Unraid can execute them repeatedly in the same xmenu window without global redeclaration collisions.
- Quality: Reset the folder editor bootstrap sentinels on every page load so the on-page runtime diagnostics reflect the current editor launch instead of stale global state.


###2026.03.25.53
- Fix: Force the folder editor page to request build-versioned runtime assets so updated `folder.js` and `folder.editor.chrome.js` cannot be masked by stale browser cache.
- Quality: Ship the page-level folder editor runtime script monitor and visible bootstrap watchdog directly from `Folder.page` so stalled editor boots surface actionable diagnostics on the live page.


